gy - Human Anatomy & Physiology September 02, 2026 Faculty Biology Department The Department of Biology at Pacific Lutheran University invites applications for a full-time, tenure-track position at the rank of Assistant Professor beginning September 1, 2027. The successful applicant will have an expertise in teaching human anatomy and physiology. The position carries a teaching load of 6 courses per year with both lecture and lab sections counting toward that total. The ... View Details Bookmark Nursing Faculty (Part-time) - Tacoma April 29, 2026 Faculty Nursing, School of PLU maintains a part-time nursing faculty pool in all areas of nursing specialties (Geriatrics, Medical/Surgical, Maternity, Mental Health, Pediatrics, and Simulation) for available assignments during the academic year.The PLU School of Nursing is dedicated to fostering a diverse and inclusive academic environment. We actively encourage applications from individuals whose backgrounds or interes... View Details Bookmark Nursing Faculty (Part-time) - Lynnwood April 29, 2026 Faculty Nursing, School of PLU maintains a part-time nursing faculty pool in all areas of nursing specialties (Geriatrics, Medical/Surgical, Maternity, Mental Health, Pediatrics, and Simulation) for available assignments during the academic year.The PLU School of Nursing is dedicated to fostering a diverse and inclusive academic environment. We actively encourage applications from individuals whose backgrounds or interes... View Details Bookmark Lecturer in Religion August 12, 2026 Faculty Religion Department The Religion Department at Pacific Lutheran University invites applications for a part-time lecturer position to teach one section of Health and Healing in Christian History (RELI 229). This course will be taught online and asynchronously in January-term 2027, and open only to students enrolled in PLU’s Accelerated Bachelor of Science in Nursing (ABSN) program. The successful candidate will hav... View Details Bookmark Copyr